`defer` schedules the cleanup to happen when the **function** returns, not when the loop iteration ends. So in your code, all the file handles accumulate and stay open until the entire function finishes. If you're iterating over many files, you'll quickly exhaust the system's file descriptor limit.

The fix is to explicitly close the file in each iteration instead of deferring:

```go
for _, f := range files {
    fh, _ := os.Open(f)
    // ... do something with fh ...
    fh.Close()
}
```

Or wrap the loop body in a function so defer closes happen per-iteration:

```go
for _, f := range files {
    func() {
        fh, _ := os.Open(f)
        defer fh.Close()
        // ... do something with fh ...
    }()
}
```

